editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-005/review-editorial.md:119:## Repair brief
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-005/review-editorial.md:121:1. **Resolve the protected countdown against the live calendar.** **Location:** Chapter 37, the board paragraph (“Sixteen days to the final”) and closing inventory (“Semester evaluation in seventeen days”); compare the book-map protected “nine weeks,” the packet close, and Chapter 30's fewer-than-six-weeks line. **Observed issue:** the manuscript is internally coherent, but it violates exact protected wording because the protected wording and movement chronology cannot both be true. **Effect on the reader:** the immediate countdown is clear now, but later inspection/final timing will expose whichever authority is left unreconciled and weaken trust in the book's carefully measured calendar. **Proposed scope:** obtain one owner/coordinator ruling; then synchronize only the affected countdown/protected line and the corresponding planning record. If “nine weeks” remains exact, the earlier Fiske-to-birthday calendar needs restaging; do not make a one-line swap. **Strength to preserve:** the entire birthday inventory, “we built ready,” and the pressure of the approaching evaluation.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-005/review-editorial.md:123:2. **Restore the authoritative movement handoff and naming gate.** **Location:** Chapter 30's “Twelve boxes”; Chapter 31 sign-up sheet and every “Gwen” use in Chapters 32–36. **Observed issue:** Brom enters at fourteen of nineteen, not twelve, and Gwen remains pending with an explicit role-placeholder instruction. **Effect on the reader:** neither error harms the local scenes, but both turn controlled continuity into accidental canon and create avoidable downstream cleanup. **Proposed scope:** reconcile Brom's count and the timing of number nineteen at four exercises per week; secure owner approval for Gwen or replace the name with the required role description until approved. **Strength to preserve:** Brom's steady four-per-week progress and every beat of the second-year's eye-drawing, pastry-aunt, dog-counting comic voice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-005/review-editorial.md:125:3. **Widen sentence architecture only in abstract explanatory passages.** **Location:** Chapter 30's file/audit rationale; Chapter 31's council and Log; Chapters 35–36's integration comparison, idle-state explanation, and working-ledger setup. **Observed issue:** mean sentence length passes the working range and long-sentence share is healthy, but SD 11.47 is far below ≈26, FRE 87.6 is far above 72.3, and FK 4.41 is below 6.8; meanwhile paragraph median 29 already sits at the accepted ceiling. **Effect on the reader:** the prose can sound syntactically younger than its ideas while still asking the listener to retain several layers of abstract reasoning. **Proposed scope:** sentence-by-sentence only: join adjacent clipped explanations that are one thought, allow a few more clearly subordinated sentences and precise multisyllabic terms, and cut true restatement rather than scene substance. Do not alter dialogue, protected wording, the fragment notice, scene breaks, or the three-night operation. **Strength to preserve:** the short landing beats, audio clarity, exact physical suspense, and warm simplicity of Chapter 37.
