editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:488:His clerk was a brisk young woman with her sleeves rolled to the elbow. She took his papers, scanned them, and turned them face up on the desk in a single smooth motion. Copper-tier certification from a registered Arbiter station. Iron Skin Path. A clean record of two seasons' documented circuit work, with Vell's stamp at the bottom of every page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:652:He had been described in bad faith before. In Denvash. In the market square. In a hundred small moments on the circuit before Vell's ledger gave people something better to go on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:668:Beneath the category, in smaller type, a printed note explained what the category was. It was reserved for any prospective practitioner who *has not yet undergone formal Kindling assessment*. The note went on. Such students were usually children whose families had asked for early schooling before their certification appointments. The category granted lecture attendance and training under supervision. It granted academic standing. It did not grant a Path, a tier, a rank, or an Arbiter-issued record of any kind.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:680:"I underwent it," he said. His voice came out quieter than he meant it to. "I was fourteen. Denvash. There's a record."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:686:"There's a record with a classification on it that the Compact's own schedule doesn't define." She said it evenly. She did not soften it. She had never softened anything she'd said to him. "This category exists for anyone without a standard classification issued by an Arbiter. The provision's language says exactly that. A child who hasn't Kindled has no standard classification. Neither do you. Yours isn't standard. It isn't anything the schedule accounts for at all."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:874:He read it over. It was not long. Hesk's letters were never long either. He folded it, wrote the Denvash direction on the outside, and set it on the desk to post in the town below.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:888:## CHAPTER — editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-03.md
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:890:# Chapter 3 — The Ledger
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:928:"Advancement," the instructor went on. Tap. "Some of you will reach Rank Ten in a tier while you're with us. When you do, your instructor will certify the rank, and you will walk down the hill to the certification station in the town, which is a registered Arbiter station, and you will be evaluated. If the evaluation confirms it, you cross. If it doesn't, you come back and keep working, and nobody here will think less of you for it." Tap. "Rank is earned on our floors. Tier is confirmed down there. We do not confuse the two, and neither should you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:932:He knew there was a station in every town of any size. He had walked into one in Denvash at fourteen, with Hesk's hand on his shoulder, and walked out with a word in brackets. He had not known until this moment that this hill town had one too, a half-hour's walk below the wall, where children from the observer track would go to be Kindled and students from the standard track would go to be measured, and where he would never, so far as he could see, have any reason to go at all.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1036:Cael sat in the plain chair and understood that very clearly. He could have wanted it to be warmth. An old man moved by a boy's hard luck. A kindly school. He had wanted that kind of thing once, in the year after Denvash, and it had always ended the same way.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1042:He had learned, across a year and a half, to be careful of anything that wanted him out of kindness. The certification office in Denvash had been kind on the day of his Kindling. Gentle voices. Apologetic about the classification even while they stamped it. That kindness had lasted exactly as long as the appointment, and not an hour longer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1260:## CHAPTER — editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-04.md
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1262:# Chapter 4 — One Condition at a Time
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1564:## CHAPTER — editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-05.md
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1566:# Chapter 5 — The Edges of the Room
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1600:"This chart," the instructor said, "is copied from the Compact's own schedule. The list the registry uses. Every Path an Arbiter can assign is on it. The families are ours, for teaching. The list is theirs. If your Arbiter tells you a Path, it will be one of these. If it isn't on this chart, it isn't a Path."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1612:"You *may* go up. Rank Ten is the threshold, not the door. To cross from Copper into Iron you need two things. The rank, which you earn yourself. And an evaluation at a registered Arbiter station, which confirms it. Both. Rank without evaluation stays where it is." He pointed down the Copper column. "Most people who Kindle into Copper never reach the threshold at all. They find a level that suits their life, and they stay there. Six of every ten working practitioners in Valdris are Copper. Most adults plateau somewhere in the middle of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1626:On the right he wrote: *Assumes an Arbiter. Assumes a station that will evaluate you. Assumes your Path is on the chart.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1632:"Declarations," the instructor said, a little later, "are how your Arbiter tells you what your Path has given you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1636:"Your first declaration comes at Kindling," he said. "Your Arbiter gives you your Path and your first ability together. After that, new declarations come as you climb. Not every rank brings one. Some do. You'll learn the rhythm of your own Path."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1646:"No," the instructor said. "You never have to. Your declarations are yours. Your Arbiter shows them to you and no one else. Nobody, not a parent, not a teacher, not an assessor, has the right to make you share one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1656:And he thought of his own notices, which no Arbiter had ever shown him because no Arbiter had ever been there. The rule did not reach him. There was no one to keep his notices private from except the people he chose to tell. He had told two.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1696:He knew that. Of course he knew it. He had known it since Denvash. He had a binder full of evidence that whatever he had, it was not a Path in any way this chart would recognize.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1726:He had known since orientation that she was on the track. He had not, until that moment, thought about what that meant. The category had been built for someone. It had been built for her. A guild family's daughter who wanted to sit in lectures before her Kindling, so that when her Arbiter came she would already know the shape of the chart. That was the real use of the hollow circle. He was the one borrowing it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1974:## CHAPTER — editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-06.md
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1976:# Chapter 6 — Panel Speed
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:2092:The provision was short. He had expected something longer, after an afternoon of arguments in a back room. It was barely half a page. It said that a candidate without a standard classification issued by an Arbiter might be enrolled for academic exposure and supervised training. It said such a candidate would be assessed monthly by demonstration before a panel of three. It said the candidate must demonstrate *consistent, observable practice*, and that the panel's finding should be entered in the candidate's record. And that was very nearly all.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:2158:He was quiet for a moment. He thought of the certification office in Denvash, the scrubbed floor, the clerk's gentle voice, the silence that had gone on far too long, and the word in brackets afterward that had followed him across half the continent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:2378:## CHAPTER — editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-07.md
