editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:746:# Chapter 14 — Standing Distribution
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:750:Vastin noticed it from the desk at a quarter past the second bell, because the court below his window was the one thing in the Compact's house that had never once been late in nineteen years. The man came out of his lodge at last with the paper bag and an apology in his shoulders, as if the birds had lodged a complaint against him, and they came down off the ledges in a grey shower and walked about his boots while he scattered the crumbs in his half-circle, the same half-circle as always, until the morning was set right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:754:There were three of them on the desk, in the order he had kept since before he had a desk worth the name: *in*, *held*, *done*. The long cabinet of shallow drawers ran down the wall at his left hand. The seal-press stood at the desk's corner, screwed down crooked, a little out of square with everything else in the room. He had fixed it there himself on his first morning, nineteen years ago, in a hurry, and had never straightened it. Every officer who came into the room looked at it once. None had ever mentioned it. He had come to think of it as a small test of manners that nobody knew they were sitting.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:914:It held fair copies of everything that had left this room in nineteen years, and he did not have to search long. He found one from his eleventh year here, a refusal he had sent to a field assessor who wished to add a page of his own to a review that had not asked for it. *The assessor's additional view is not contemplated by the review's terms.* One sentence. No provision cited. He laid the open book on the blotter and set the seat's sheet beside it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:948:In the outer office the clerk wrote the candle into the consumables in his tidy upright figures, against the Archmarshal's name. It would sit there as long as the ledger did: one stub of tallow, the only odd line in that room's accounts in nineteen years.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:958:The standard Arbiter protocol could not evaluate this subject. When it fell silent before him, the silence belonged to the instrument and told nothing about the man in it. A re-evaluation whose result was known before it began was a procedure wearing an evaluation's coat. And the proceedings, if they meant to evaluate at all, had one honest instrument already in their hands: three years of the demonstration record, kept under seal, by officers with eyes.
