editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5125:## Where we enter
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5129:## What this movement is for
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5131:Show the institution's reach as paper while the defense wins every point it can win: the best evaluator benched, the continent buying the question, the inventory reaching a border town's workbench, and a paragraph that says *lawful* and *proceeding* at once. The last stretch of the front-loaded first third.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5138:- **Seln's service-side circuit, walked with Cael** (new): the lodge counter, the post-room sort; "He is holding a road." The four queries; Karis's blank fifth line; **Hesk's letter**; **pre-restriction inventory** — nine weeks, the sixth; **"The question is what we do the day after."** Withrow's completed inventory, told flat: "Not a hand on the door. A hand on the clock."
