editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5549:# AUTHOR REPORT — Book 6, Movement 3 "The Evaluator and the Public Record" (chapters 14–20)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5560:## Chapters
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5564:| 14 | Standing Distribution | 5,129 | 5 | **VASTIN cutaway (whole chapter).** Day 41 in his high room in the Compact's house: the porter late with the pigeons; the three trays; the crooked seal-press screwed on nineteen years ago; the left hand that now dislikes evenings too. A bundle *For the evaluator's file, per standing distribution* — told, not asked — with the instrument, the answer's index, the seat's notice and the first sitting's minute: the proceedings have already sat. Dull papers first (his rule). Paragraph seven: his own three sentences, *adopts*. Chapter fourteen twice in forty years (a hill station keeper's false returns; a coastal officer's bought rank) and the daughter's letter, answered *no*. The nine leaves; the eleven questions; the boy's question back; **the twelfth** (what the private records say) left lying — still right, and his rightness left the proceedings only one thing of his to take. **The petition for standing**: two provisions, the older's *shall receive*; four cases in forty years, four received. The clerk's pen stops at the routing column. Day 43: **the northern junior's Kindling file** — within tolerance, *continue observation*; Vastin keeps the copy, *held*, out, *held* again, no word for it. Day 45, **the wrong step on the stair**; seat courier; pressed seal; **the two-sentence denial**; he lays his own old refusal from the letter-book beside it — the same bench. **The finding by candle**: the clerk's one non-work sentence ("Will you be getting home tonight, sir? It's set in to rain."); the candle on the consumables; nine pages, four points; the third page (the frames are not to blame — the same sentence, said for a person); the addressee line bare; the lowest drawer; ***Pending a proceeding worth sending it to.*** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5569:| 19 | The Shape | 4,687 | 5 | **Day 49 supper.** The Ternhall keeper's private letter: Karis's transfer file requested — **"That's twice."** Seln's **beans**, laid right to left: Ternhall; Velmere's provincial registry; Lira's certification at the district seat *for completeness*; the house's own counter (item four); the coats now hold the road; "One query is a clerk… Four… is somebody's plan." Lira: the Fenmark line under the corrections — "Put it in your column." Brom: **"Does the query show at the estate's end?"** — the head of his house is on the file. Karis rules **one empty line**. Two hours later **Hesk's letter** in the evening post, opened walking (the surveyor's level set back a hair wrong because the whole valley agrees with it; the widow's dog), then **read aloud at the window** — **the protected paragraph**. *Grew up in it*: the shavings under the bench, the tin box. Lira: "Denvash." Seln's fifth bean apart; Karis fills the line. **"Walking the fences" / pre-restriction inventory**: before the ruling; "Nine weeks. They are in the sixth."; five dull files, an afternoon to assemble. Karis: the ninth heading, *other relationships* — what he'd mind; Brom: "Said." Lira takes a bean: **"The question is what we do the day after."** Seln's stillness. **Withrow** reads the letter (twelve breaths; stops for nine); the brown pocket code; the haulier's story **told from the flour sack backward** — nine letters in the order they came; Force, Bronze Rank Four; the station slip twenty years old; two frames silent; seven weeks of careful work; one trouble in nine coats; east past the last station in eighteen months; the daughter at her counter; *grew up in it* under the ninth heading; **"Not a hand on the door. A hand on the clock."**; choosing, dearer tonight. Log: the first pole cracks — the line between the system and the people can't be found. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5572:## State at movement end (for the ledger)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5574:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names; feet and yards. Day 41 Sixth-day: Vastin's courtesy copy; his petition by that noon's dispatch. Day 43 First-day: the northern junior's file. **Day 44 Second-day**: the seat refuses the petition in the morning; the assistant's market errand; the counsel brings the refusal up at dusk (the house knows a day before Vastin). **Day 45 Third-day**: Vastin receives the denial (the fourth morning) and writes the finding that night; Bracken's baskets; Gault's notice; the correspondent and Rooke; the visitors' log; the piles; a Velmere letter; the fee office's query; the column filled. **Day 46 Fourth-day**: wing three under the gallery (moved from the Fifth-day for the sitting); Rooke closes the program floor; Umber's transmission. **Day 47 Fifth-day: second sitting** (the exhibits, fifty-one minutes); the release to the faculties; Daeva's statement walked up at supper. **Day 48**: Daeva's letter in the post-room sort; Lira at the rail. **Day 49 Seventh-day** (last day of the inventory's sixth week): the lodge book; "holding a road"; the four queries and the Ternhall letter at supper; Hesk's letter; pre-restriction inventory named; Withrow's story. **Day 51 Second-day**: the honest floor. **Day 54 Fifth-day: the third sitting, the preliminary** — sustained on validity, sustained to full proceedings. Lira's first road meet is day ~63. Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5582:- **Cael and the circle:** Vastin petitioned for standing and was refused in two sentences without citation (the circle has the sentences verbatim from the counsel; they do not know of his finding, his candle or his drawer). The two old provisions. Umber's covering note. Daeva's statement (public) — and her private letter (Cael only; Lira knows a letter came, not its text). The four queries and the fifth (Denvash). Pre-restriction inventory: nine weeks, in the sixth on day 49. Withrow's haulier and the nine headings. The coats now hold the road. The preliminary's ruling and Ilsev's minuted scope. Nothing about falsification, the sub-layer, a maker, [UNBOUND] or Tide. The returns' wording still unknown. Cael knows nothing of Havel's note.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5593:- **Hesk's newest letter** (the surveyor's level; the dog; the protected paragraph).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5627:- File designations unchanged. The inventory (unserved, unnamed on any paper) runs to about day 70.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5640:- (e) The Seln circuit is walked on days 48 (post sort) and 49 (lodge), and the four queries, Hesk's letter, the inventory and Withrow's story all fall on day 49, so the inventory is named inside its sixth week. The source's "four days" between the queries and Hesk's letter became two hours.
