editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5672:- **The beans** (Seln's "A drawing can be found. Beans can be eaten.") and "walking the fences" as the monitoring office's slang for a pre-restriction inventory.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5674:## Protected and packet lines used
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5676:Verbatim from BOOK_MAP §8 (Tier A / Tier B):
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5681:- *Two polite men from the registry came through Denvash asking after my trade licenses and the shop's title. Wanted to know if you had any interest recorded in either. I told them my grandson's interest in this shop is that he grew up in it, and they wrote that down. Whatever they're building, it has a shape. Mind the shape. — H.* (ch19)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5686:**Proposed patterns for `protected-patterns.txt`:** none required — `ed.sh overlap` reads **0 unprotected runs** with the file as it stands (15 protected runs allowed via BOOK_MAP). If the coordinator wants the packet lines guarded anyway, the two packet-quoted lines of eight or more words are `the question is what we do the day after` and `now you understand the file i.ve been reading my whole career`.
