editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5702:## Formula (formula_metrics.py, ch14–20, after the last edit)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5737:**Progression vocabulary.** Strict subset (tier/rank/rating/bracket/exhibition/Arbiter/classif\*/fragment/burst/provision/evaluat\*/notice/advancement/sitting/panel/band/rate/covenant/anomaly/enrollment/enrollee/nullification/suspension/restriction/drill-book/integration/flag/exchange/declaration and the metal tiers): 244 hits, **≈72 per 10k** (M2 also ≈72). With Path and fragment words (read, give, spark, lane, Storm, Wind, Path, Kindling, frame, figure) it is well above the first-third target of ~83. Densest: ch17 (the band bout; the exhibits) and ch20 (the honest floor; the preliminary). Thinnest: ch16 and ch19. Combat vocabulary: ≈26 per 10k (strike/blow/touch/guard/palm/forearm/bout/exchange/glide/sweep), present outside the two floors (Ephram's woodcut, the Current, Lira's drills).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5745:## Owner flags
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5747:1. **Seln and Shadow (coordinator ruling not applied).** The task's standing ruling says Seln learns why Shadow was sealed "in Book 6 Ch15, in this movement, as the plan and Book 5's ledger reserve it", and to follow the packet for how much. Every source I can find places that telling at **source** Book 6 Ch15, *The Cache*: BOOK_MAP §3 item 15 ("Cael tells Seln the mechanism; the Shadow seal and its cost; 'You kept my file too, then.'"), §6 (Seln "does not know a sealed thing exists until M6"), §9 (the integration mechanism "Expands to Seln only (M6)"), and B5's BOOK_MAP/packets ("B6 Ch15 tells him", meaning the source chapter). Edition chapter 15 is in M3, which may be the source of the confusion. The M3 packet calls for no telling at all ("Seln's method shown; his case not mentioned aloud"), and telling him why Shadow is sealed would require telling him the integration mechanism four movements early, and would strand the Tier A line "You kept my file too, then." So **Seln is not told in M3**. If the owner does want it here, it needs a packet line, and the cache scene in M6 will need replanning.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5748:2. **Calendar.** Vastin's petition day 41 → refusal at Ostrand day 44 → received day 45; the house hears on day 44 (from the counsel). Second sitting day 47; preliminary day 54. The inventory's sixth week is days 43–49, and it is named on day 49. Please confirm against "the first term, middle weeks".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5773:The canon check found one concrete continuity defect: the Movement 3 Velmere letter is opened immediately, but the binding forward plan identifies the second letter of the year as the unopened letter carried toward Movement 7. Everything else—calendar, bodies, power costs, knowledge limits, protected text, and source-reuse gate—holds. I’m writing the review with that as the mandatory repair and keeping the formula recommendation narrowly scoped.
