editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold.md:1:# Cold read — Book 3, Movement 1 (chapters 1–8)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold.md:7:**Series position:** this is the opening of a third book. I read it as both a returning reader (who knows Ardenmere, Vell, Hesk, Denvash, the Ironyard) and a new one (who knows none of that) and note where the two diverge.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold.md:11:## 1. Unscored reader response
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-cold.md:35:**Orientation, returning vs. new reader.** A returning reader is well oriented: the Power Log pass in ch. 1 (lines 191–222) is a recap disguised as a habit, and it works. A new reader can follow: every offstage name is given a function on its first use (Vell = circuit ledger, Hesk = letter, Denvash = Kindling, Fenmark = expulsion). The cost is that ch. 1–2 carry roughly a dozen offstage proper nouns, and a new reader holds three unexplained plants by ch. 6 ("Session nine," "the stranger's note from Ardenmere," the "four cases"). None of these block understanding; all three are opaque enough that a new reader may assume they are things they should already know rather than things being withheld on purpose.
