editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:33:## 3. Scored dimensions (editorial judgments, not measurements)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:52:## 4. Canon, state, limits, knowledge, reserved disclosures
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:56:### 4.1 Verified correct (no action)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:58:- Wray is a woman throughout (BOOK_MAP §12.1) ✓. "Iron Skin" in full everywhere ✓. Cael fifteen and never aged (ch5 "two years older than the oldest" thirteen-year-olds) ✓. Residence wing, Lira two doors down, Brom across the corridor ✓. No Karis, no Ternhall, no Coss on the page (the imagined reader in ch6 is a nameless composite), no Level 4, no routing code ✓. Pressure and Compression never reach any record ✓. No "before Arbiters" / "before the registry" language around the archive ✓ (Prynn: "From before this was a school").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:59:- Tier colours, Platinum "historical", Void "a word in stories", and the 60/25/10/4/<1 proportions match the Universe Bible ✓. Every Path named on the chart (Wind, Current, Storm, Stone, Iron Skin, Shield, Anchor, Wall, Blade, Glass, Ember, Ash, Force, Pressure, Mire, Tide) exists in canon files ✓ — no new Path was invented. Naveth's career (eleven years, a decade between, Greyvane years unnumbered) per §12.2 ✓. Standings by term record within cohort; Lira's opponent "high on the Copper side" per §12.21 ✓. Edran Iron R2, third year ✓.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:62:### 4.2 Findings
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:64:**F1 — Reveal pacing: Cael already holds the acquisition correlation (ch6, "Then he went through the binder").** The text reads: "And under all four, the thing that was not a fragment at all. How any of them had come to him. The fact that each had arrived after he had watched someone use their Path, closely, under real stakes." STATE_LEDGER (Cael — knowledge): *Believes: fragments "arrive" like weather. Does not know: that acquisition can be aimed.* BOOK_MAP §10 releases "observation is necessary but not sufficient; genuine engagement completes it" through Karis's hypothesis (M3), the nulls (M4) and the match (M5); the packet's M3 beat is "Cael's two days: weather or appetite." Here Cael states the observation-plus-stakes pattern as a fact in week one. It is never disclosed to anyone and never recorded, so this is **plan adherence / reveal pacing, not a canon disclosure** — but it pre-empts the discovery arc that two later movements are built on. Scope: keep "How any of them had come to him" and the "Never" decision; drop "under real stakes" and the causal "after he had watched someone use their Path, closely," in favour of what he actually knows (each has a source person; he does not know why; it feels like weather).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:66:**F2 — Prynn's tenure (ch6, archive).** "Three times in thirty years." Canon anchor (BOOK_MAP §9.2, ch17): "Sixty years I've kept these shelves"; STATE_LEDGER: "sixty years with the shelves." Change thirty to sixty (or make the thirty refer to something else, e.g. since the provision was written).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:74:**F6 — "A year and a half" (ten uses across ch1, ch3, ch6, ch8).** BOOK_MAP §12.16 asks the author to avoid restating it where the sentence does not need it, because the series calendar cannot hold it. Not a canon error; a trim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:76:**F7 — Pending names used in prose (ch3 onward: Oona; ch5: Gerda; ch8: Hobb).** The packet and BOOK_MAP §13 say to use the bracketed role until the owner approves. The author discloses this. Owner decision needed; if any name is refused, the ch8 drill-board discovery of "Hobb" needs rework rather than a find-and-replace. **Plan adherence.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:78:**F8 — Source-sentence reuse (brief compliance).** EDITION_BRIEF: "The prose is new… Read them for events, not for sentences"; the formula section: "No source novel quotations." Method: both texts normalised (lower case, punctuation stripped), every run of ten or more consecutive words shared between a manuscript chapter and source ch1–4 / book-02 ch24 listed, runs containing BOOK_MAP protected or §9.2 anchor wording excluded (script saved in my scratchpad as overlap2.py). Result: **40 unprotected shared runs of ≥10 words**, by chapter 3 / 3 / 11 / 3 / 2 / 5 / 10 / 3. The author's disclosed echo-repair covered ch1–2 (which are nearly clean); chapters 3, 6 and 7 were not swept. Longest and most visible:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:86:### 4.3 Reader Standard (EDITION_BRIEF; VOICE_CHARTER end section)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:89:### 4.4 Audio-first (VOICE_CHARTER §8) and tic caps (§9)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:91:- §9 phrase caps: all book-level capped phrases at 0 ("That was true" once). Single-word paragraphs within cap. **"the way a…" identical construction: ch7 has seven (cap three per chapter)**; "the way he/she…" reaches four in ch6 and ch8. "very" runs at ~36 per 10k. The scene-closer rule: ch4 (log entry) and ch5 (binder opened on a clean page) are consecutive log-shaped closers; ch6 and ch8 both close on falling asleep with ch7 between (allowed).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:92:- Names by ear: Hobb / Hesk / Havel and Oona / Quenna are the only near pairs; BOOK_MAP §13 already screened both.
