editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1154:    37	The pre-restriction inventory: five offices, complete, executed at a tempo that meant staffing, which meant budget, which meant authorization at an altitude no district controlled. He had run three inventories in his career and had never had more than two clerks for any of them, and two clerks had taken nine weeks for a man with a wife and a workshop. Five offices in six weeks against a delegation, an academy, three provincial registries and a border town was not a clerk's tempo. It was an office's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1174:    57	The operative's catechism, learned in his first posting, proved in all nineteen: insurance is only insurance while it stays sealed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1181:    64	*Nobody has ever protected a man by believing him.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1183:    66	The case's whole value — to him, to anyone — lay in its being closed. A keeper with a sealed case was a man with a price on his silence that no one knew they were paying, which was the only kind of price that stayed paid. Fifteen years of it had bought him nineteen postings, a clean separation from a service that did not do clean separations, and a desk at a mid-tier academy where nobody had ever asked him a question he could not answer flatly.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1203:    86	A table with a place at it that nobody had ever announced. He had counted, once, how many tables he had sat at in nineteen postings where the chair had been *his* rather than *a* chair, and the count was one, and the counting had annoyed him for a week.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1205:    88	A Gold-tier match, in front of the whole continent, fought at the edge of what the boy had, with something held back and sealed the entire time to protect a cover whose owner had never been told it was being protected. He had worked that out afterward, alone, from the shape of what had not happened on that floor, and had sat with the finding for an hour, and had told nobody, and had not been thanked, and had not wanted to be, and had understood exactly what he had been handed and by whom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1217:   100	It came off the shelf in his quarters the way it had come off nineteen shelves in nineteen postings — a plain locked traveling case, scuffed at the corners, the least remarkable object he owned, which was its whole design. It weighed eleven pounds. It had a maker's stamp inside the lid that belonged to a firm that had gone out of business twenty years ago, which was the second-best thing about it, and no maker's mark anywhere on the outside, which was the first. He had carried it through customs at two border stations, through a fire at an inn, and past a records office he had been burgling, and had never once had to explain it, because a mild administrative man with a case is not a question anyone forms.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1243:   126	He manufactured the schedule gap himself: a floor-inventory session, entered in the office's own calendar in the office's own hand, annex closed for cataloguing, the entry so ordinary that the office's other clerk initialed it without reading it. It was the ninth such entry he had made that term. The other eight had been genuine floor inventories, conducted, minuted, and filed, and he had made them for a year and a half for no reason except that a pattern is only cover if it existed before you needed it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1568:   131	The inventory went into the satchel's first use that night, at the window, the new leather's smell in the room and the fountain running below, and it was the fullest the log had ever carried:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:1570:   133	*Eight confirmed fragments. Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — Feryn. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — source protected, deployment none, ever, anywhere; the seal's third year begins. Storm-adjacent — Daeva; settled, resettled twice this week around the new neighbor, holding. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; two days integrated; idle state learned; the doorways have stopped raising their hands, and I have entered in the deployment notes the first honest sentence about it: I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people, taken from a hand with no face, and I have not yet decided what it is for, and the not-deciding is entered as a decision.*
