editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:2510:    89	Seln had lived in nineteen towns, and every one of them had a man like that, who looked at the water for a living and was right about it twice a year.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:2755:    75	It was four lines. Every man in the service learned them in his first year, and said them under his breath on the first morning of every posting, the way other men touched a doorpost for luck. Seln had said them nineteen times on nineteen first mornings. He had never once said them on any other morning, because there had never been any other morning that needed them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:2767:    87	*Nobody has ever protected a man by believing him.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:2781:   101	He had believed the last line more than the other three together. It was the one that had kept him clean. You did not protect a subject by believing him; you protected him by counting what he did, and filing it true, and letting the true thing be your only argument. He had never believed anybody in his life. He had counted them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:2787:   107	*Nobody has ever protected a man by believing him.* It was true. He had never seen it done. He was going to try.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:3401:   199	He could feel the lines now, faintly, through the read. They ran from the point on his coat out to the nineteen round him, and from the nineteen out to the fourteen in the cut, and from all of them, all of them, back to her. She stood on her flat patch of crown fifteen feet away with every line in the cut running into her two loose hands like the reins of a team.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:3425:   223	Every course in the cut stood out to him as plainly as the chalk dust had stood out along his lane: taut grey threads in the air, from point to point to point, a great slack net laid down the whole length of the road, closed at both ends, open in one channel where Brom stood. He saw the nineteen round him, each with its line to the next. He saw the one against his coat, the first stitch, with every other line in the cage worked through it. And he saw how it was held. It was held from inside, from where it touched him. It was the same thing as the point at his breastbone and the one under the horse's leg and the ones that held the coachman's hands. It was a thing set against a surface and told to stay.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:3431:   229	It went the way you let go of a breath you have been holding without knowing it. The point against his coat was simply not there any more. And because every other point in the cage had been laid through it, they went after it, one after another, in the order she had laid them, unthreading round him in a quick soft ripple like a row of stitches coming out when the first is pulled. The nineteen went. Their lines went out to the fourteen in the cut, and the fourteen went too. He felt them go down the road behind him like a rope paying out over a wheel: the three across the west mouth, the two in the south bank's lip, the three high in the north bank, the parapets, the milestone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:3762:The probe’s hot spots are not automatically findings. Several exact or high-similarity pairs are explicitly protected or packet-supplied (the catechism, Anchor notice, Hesk note, and “room was never the system”), so I’m excluding those and testing the surrounding prose for independently inherited sentence logic and beat order.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:4134:    43	"From Denvash," he said. "Carrier's mark from the far end of the country, nine days on the road. It's been rained on twice. The inside should be dry; whoever packed it knew what he was about." He weighed it on his palm a moment, by habit. "A little under three pounds."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:4316:   225	He took the book out of its pocket and opened it to a clean leaf and wrote the inventory, because a birthday was as good a day as any to count what he carried.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/source-tracking.stdout.log:4350:   259	He wrote one more line, under the inventory, and blotted it, and put the book back in its pocket in the satchel, and buckled the flap.
