editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:832:| 21 | The Landing | 4,414 | 5 | **LIRA cutaway (~1,970).** Way in: the second carter's "You buying a wagon or selling one?" Her rule from the floor — never the same corner twice; three errands that are real; the grey coats look past her (insulted, then glad). Carter one (day 58, mules): manifests stamped at every station, then a gap at the paper's edge; "nobody with a book". Carter two (day 61, a woman with good horses and a Mire daughter): fords, four days loaded / three light, the bad well; "Nobody's got a book to write you in." Carter three (day 64, young, a new wagon): exactly where the last station stands — "I turn there." The sum at the second switchback; the meet card re-chalked eight days later (the confluence's repairs); the ladder; her oath to leave rooms on her own feet, and the next room one she loves. The note. **Cael, day 66:** the board; Seln at the copying table — "Five drawers. Full. Shut." (the seals change color). Lira on the north wall at dusk: "Fifth-day"; the meet put back; "Does it cost you much? The band." / "Like a toll." **Day 68, the small room** (an old dairy, slate shelves, a joiner's table that leaves as firewood): Brom with the good chair — "It's for the council." Lira: "Why do we keep answering them?" — the carters as a sum; the third "Turns round at it." **Karis** stands and reads the second paragraph of a coastal default ruling first (the respondent's own letter quoted as proof); *fled*; her other column (Norhold's clause, Bracken's book, Greyvane, Vell's ledger; Denvash with nothing written); Brom: "Was it wrong?" "It was true." "The machine has a form for leaving." **Seln's one correction**: forty days after the fourth sitting's close; the code counts days, not sittings. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:833:| 22 | Both Roads | 4,790 | 5 | Brom tips the chair: **"Prepare both roads." "Win the sittings. Keep a box."** — Lira counts three. The word *box* stays. Shirts, all the strapping, the plaque ("If I leave it, you'll go back for it"); hand to the LEFT pocket; **"It's the second box that's the problem."** — the sealed letter, twenty-three days; nobody asks. **Cael's first pole at full strength**, from the bottom: Pellin as a woman with a brass plate, eleven seconds, fourteen; forward through Vell, Greyvane, the grant and two renewals on paper, the inspection, Norhold's clause, Umber's *no number goes here*; "People change with the weather. Text doesn't." **"I'm not leaving the room while the text still works."** He pre-empts the objection; "always Karis who read it." **Karis names it an induction** (a run; "Every rule anybody ever broke looked exactly like this the evening before"; a tally, not a guarantee). **Lira: Fenmark's perfect form; "It's not ground. It's a floor."**; joists somebody laid; *Both roads* — it costs Cael nothing and nobody makes him pay. Seln's two looks. The slow spirit kettle; Karis: "Memory improves things"; **"It was the night we asked."** Seln lights them up the dairy step and crosses to the wing. Log. **SELN cutaway (~2,330), the dark wing**: no lamp, the fire-watch's square on the counter; his one correction examined (forty days as a narrow door); fifteen years, nineteen postings, sixty-three subjects, the followed few; the maintenance records copied twelve years ago on his fourth posting, understood in a green corridor between two appointments — *whose question it had been*; the boy inferred (the mill-town table; two slips burned on the coals; a season that never settled; Norhold spent on purpose); his own true, empty reports filed with the boy's receipts; the brass key held and returned; the dairy step and the lamp he held for each of them; ***The deciding has stopped being quiet.*** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:836:| 25 | The Rail | 4,682 | 6 | Seln's head turns first; **the production order** — an officer in grey with a case held before him, the clerk carrying nothing; **fifty-one seconds** counted along the north benches, the hall turning from the Current girl's bout; *the complete records of evaluation-linked floor work of the enrollee of record, Caelen Hesk-ward*; Bracken reads it standing, signs, takes the duplicate; **Withrow thanks the officer by full grade** to four rows. Lawful in every line; "The hour is not in the order." **The hall's regard adjusting**: applause taken back to be weighed; the steward; two correspondents out. Lira at the rope: "They waited… Till I'd lost well"; the boy's card and his mother. Supper: **Seln's clerk** on the south benches since the first bell, out at the second touch, back with the officer nineteen minutes later; "They waited for the hall"; Withrow: bind the records "in the house's own boards… they may look at it handsomely." **LIRA cutaway (~1,770), day 72**: the corridor of trestles; the Silver — "go on your fifth"; "Because you'd asked"; the town and its licences; the finals' politeness. Evening rail: the steward's sheet *for your file*; the ladder counted rung by rung (Iron Rank One; 27 in the red book; one point under a hall's seal; the Stone; Zerin's *Silver bracket. Next cycle.*; the corridor); four nights since the dairy; no Silver card past the stamps. Cael with the order's duplicate. **"One of these is the best night of my life." / "Noted."** The folds won't lie the same way twice; it will go in the box. Home in rain; the watcher looks at the colors trunk; log: *They can't touch the paper. The paper's honest. So they choose the hour.* |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:840:## State at movement end (for the ledger)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:850:- **The circle:** the road east as Lira's sum (the last Arbiter station four days past Ostrand loaded, three light; stamps stop there; two carters go past, the third turns at it and won't say why); the coastal default and *fled*; forty days after the fourth sitting's close; the five offices' inventories closed (Seln); Jent's sentence on the record; the fossil provision's two paragraphs (the second kept unmentioned); the escort order whole; a "facilities office" nobody can place; **Anchor Path** as a name and a use (rare; service; enforcement; holds people) — **inferred only: no range, rate or cost**; the three-way distinction (Ternhall's anchors / the Lattice Path / Anchor Path).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:891:- **Escort order (day 76):** *In the matter of Caelen Hesk-ward.* + the Tier B body; a "facilities office" newly constituted; declined pending verification; no written refusal demanded; logged. Bracken to write to the district seat.
