editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:4766:    43	*They didn't score me low. They didn't score me high. They couldn't score me. I have spent three years telling myself I can beat anyone at my tier. Tonight the fairest instrument ever built agreed with the Arbiter, the brackets, and the registry: I am not at any tier.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:4808:    85	"Fifty-one minutes," she said, so that only he heard. "That's what mine took. At the station, with the Arbiter." She put the pot down. "Make of that what you like."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:4851:/bin/zsh -lc "find editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand -name 'protected-patterns.txt' -o -name '*protected*' -maxdepth 3 -print
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:4862:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-26.md:103:They were from the dairy. He had written them on the way down in the coach that morning, out of habit, to have the argument by him in case anybody in that room should ever ask him for it: Denvash and the brass plate; Vell's ledger; the Greyvane hearing; the grant and two renewals on paper; the inspection; the clause at Norhold; Umber's *no number goes here*. His receipts. He had laid them out a week ago, in order, at full strength, and Karis had called them an induction and he had not had an answer for her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r3.stdout.log:4868:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-22.md:63:Cael did not need to be told what was under the hand. A square cream envelope with a dark red seal on it, unbroken, which had come up the hill twenty-three days ago and had not been opened since. Under it, the summons, the docket, the district's confirmation with *outcome anticipated* on it in a clerk's round hand, and a sitting on the last Fifth-day of the year at which three assessors and a sigil frame would almost certainly find Brom an Iron. His family's ledger had been waiting for that line since before he could lift a practice weight. In the second box was a grandmother at the head of a long table, and a word he had never once said in the same breath as *east*.
