editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-005/compiled-prompt.md:623:The carriers' hut was busy. The west bag was hanging on its hook on the back wall, half full, with WEST painted on it in tall black letters, and the clerk with the inky fingers was behind the counter weighing a parcel on the little brass balance. Cael waited his turn. He thought about the old woman in the shawl saying *because the clerk is young and thinks it's clever to know things*, and looked at the clerk, who was perhaps nineteen and had ink on his cuff as well as his fingers, and who was not looking at anybody in particular.
