editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:331:## What this movement is for
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:333:Silver is not a bigger Iron, and the first pole cracks at the book's midpoint. Then a day when nobody is measured. Then the found family fights together on a sanctioned floor for the first time, and meets a Gold-tier fact that does not fit any unit's argument. The last third begins here. Teaching surfaces only at turning points: the weave's depth, the inventory at seventeen, the read at its limit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:337:- **Cael vs the Rhagen Shield captain (~4,800)** per BOOK_MAP §8. The weave takes probes like deep water, and the renewal has no rhythm to time; the Norhold block's Shield lesson [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05: "winter" dropped] voids in one exchange. The displacement game; the captain re-anchors on the crown; a handspan, twice, with footwork no dossier documents; Compression banked at contact; Ember knocks one layer off tempo; the fourth exchange. The captain: "We could not find the edges of you." The costs: the left hip flexor (four days) and channel-burn on the right hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:338:- **The circle's debrief:** Lira itemizes the invented footwork; Brom: "The absorption stayed banked." Karis: "The doctrine isn't failing. The doctrine is *filling*." **The midpoint log** (protected), written slowly.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:343:- **The new volume's first entry:** the inventory at seventeen, with six fragments and their notes, "Still open. Still real. Patience." Use "a year, near enough" / "since the records hall" for the Shadow fragment's age (C9) [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05: replaces "since last spring" — season word; acquired on the stair, B4 d149/150]. Its Shadow line records the SECOND year of "useful where: nowhere yet" (B4 ch62), not the third [audit B4]. The inventory's other lines count from B4 ch62 a year on (Wind six free, the landing beat four years; Compression three years and still no official eye; Ember four instants; Pressure flat at two plates and one travelling evaluation).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:344:- **The trial draw:** HALCENVANE — AUREMONT. Ternhall's raised cup; the criers with no price on the fifth name; Karis lays the squad clause on the rail: "The clause does the rest. Again." The log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:347:- **The team trial semifinal (~7,000)** per §8: the morning inspection (the joint gaps; the blind middle third; "fast north, slow south"; Cael alone notes the diagonal as *the feature nobody has priced*). Two exchanges as the better unit (Ephram declines the south platform; Brom in the second joint; Karis's ramps; Lira's one word). **Ilsev cutaway (~700):** her pen stops at the break. Third exchange: **the stormlane down the diagonal.** Everyone is visited in sequence, and the read at its absolute limit gives him half a second. **She stops for one full second and looks at him the way he looks at things.** Fourth exchange: they re-form. Zerin declines an unpriced trade. Auremont advances on objectives. The Concourse stands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:348:- **Aftermath:** Rooke ("The third exchange wasn't a squad problem"); Ephram's handshake (protected; "It had four more sentences and Lira cut them"); the log. Lira: "Third-place trial first."
