editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:1254:### Bodies
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:1258:| Cael | Sixteen (turned on the eleventh of Sowing, Book 4; the date is never set beside a season word, OWNER #35). Healthy, rested, and trained: sixty-one floor sessions over the recess. No current injuries: B4 closed him fit (the quarter-burst's hip load ended the night of the twenty-third of Reaping; the plate's right-shoulder ache eased by the week's end). The leading hip carries the Wind fragment's old strain (crest to inner knee after a hard evening), and the landing beat is still unshortened. The right shoulder pays Pressure, "four blows a sitting", the circle's private cap and not a registry schedule (B4 ch62; OWNER #36: the plate/Pressure shoulder is the right). The Shadow fragment's rent runs from waking, spent or not; drifts come in the gaps, never in the work, and the weekly count is falling; the working ledger's day count since the stair and the protocol *Hold. First.* are the discipline. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:1259:| Lira | Wind Path, Iron-tier, Rank One, formal: the Ostrand registry station's Arbiter evaluation on the fifth of the new month, fifty-one minutes ("They didn't give me anything today. They caught up."); the porter changed the word and moved her name the next day; Gault filed, Ilsev witnessing. Season record certified "Eleven bouts unbeaten. None lost." The Copper Crown is retired on the shelf over the settle ("There. It's retired."). Fit: the semifinal's hip strain (deep, nothing torn) had a month's knitting left at term's end, and nothing of it carries into this book. She trains at dawn on Rooke's speed line. She meant to write to Fiske over the recess (Fiske: "North tier, next season. I'll be watching the Iron bracket."); whether she did is open to M1–M3. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:1260:| Brom | Iron Skin Path, Copper formal ("until somebody filed for him"); Iron-grade in practice. Third in Rooke's cohort; lost the Copper final to Lira by one beat in the fourth exchange, on the mended seam. The force-redirect seam is repaired (Rooke's nineteen exercises, four a week; he stops finishing the absorption and drives while still hard on the struck side). Recess sheet: "Nineteen. Round three. Four a week." Fit; the final's iced knee and strapped right knuckles are B4's and do not carry. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:1264:| Hesk | At home in Denvash, his workshop "at the far end of the country" (B4 ch62). His last letter came by the evening coach on the twelfth: "…wrote 'keep looking.' In my day that was called respect… Sixteen suits you." (his guess from Cael's own letter, not knowledge; OWNER #10). Writes on "a war footing": nine letters in twelve weeks (B5's own; not in B4). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:1265:| Vastin | The Archmarshal Vastin (his B4 title throughout, ch38–59). Last seen in B4 at the posting-house at the turn of the registry road on the evening of the twenty-fourth of Reaping, writing the file note and a four-sentence private letter to Bracken. His desk in the Compact's western administration (third floor, river side) is the source's, not B4's, and stands only until the text says otherwise. **No stated age** (§12 C2; OWNER #8, #17); career "forty years". His left hand "had begun to dislike evenings as well as mornings". [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:1267:### Knowledge
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:1269:**Cael knows:** his six fragments, with their costs and deployment rules (the ch62 inventory: "Six and an anomaly. It isn't a seventh anything."); that the mechanism is integration of witnessed abilities under the stakes conditions; the line the four signed at Halcenvane the year before, the minute of three numbered rules (conditions not manufactured; a directed acquisition only within earnest engagement the other party begins, awake and directed; full cost written beforehand), for which *directed, open-eyed, or not at all* is this book's shorthand and never B4's wording; that Seln has functionally switched (the corridor on the twenty-seventh; the unchanged rotations; the recess counter sheet) and that "Gratitude is the leak"; that one unsigned slip of wing paper came to him inside a returned coursework folder on the night of the Copper final, learned and burned on the common-room coals, and that he and Karis alone know it; that Vastin wrote a note he believes says he is not an error (inferred, not seen; OWNER #10; "in a hand I'd wager signs its whole name"); that the Level 4 designation exists and nobody can trace it; that the fielding clause exists, with its text verbatim (sixth part, subsection four); the year's finding, "The system isn't confused about me"; and the tournament's three-year cycle and Norhold as this cycle's host. He does **not** know the Standard's mechanics yet (that comes in the map room); the exhibition provision's wording; the squad clause; Daeva beyond rumor; what Seln's reports said; or anything about the office above Vastin. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
