editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:1285:- **Delegation:** two wagons; travel roster of eleven (five competitors, Rooke, Gault, two third-year reserves, a wagoner, and S. Seln for *records and floor scheduling*). The roster line carries the registry name *Caelen Hesk-ward, 41-7843-V* once, so the schedule office's "C. Cael" reads as its abbreviation (§10 item 6). Fourteen of the hill's students are Silver and one is Gold (B4 ch8), and none is fielded; M1 says why in one sentence. Withrow and Bracken travel for the fourth meet and Norhold. Bracken's pouch is the delegation's letter route from Movement 3 on (Karis's information policy). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
