editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-005/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:12:## Chapters
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-005/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:16:| 28 | The Thin File | 4,694 | **Coss cutaway, the whole chapter.** Day 51, evening: the **fourth reading** at the borrowed desk upstairs at the post, the left front leg rocking, the folded paper that has slipped from under it. **Attention over brilliance** (the brilliant deskmate sent to copy reports on the coast). The six sheets: registration (Pellin, Weaver's Row), the Statute 14 notice, a passive **gate entry** (Denvash Outer gate, eastbound, day 3), the sweep request, the sweep's one-line return (Torvin's, resident, nothing observed), his own brief. **What a [SHATTERED]-class file should hold and this one doesn't**: preliminary risk assessment, residential note, review cross-reference, a case number, a handler. "It was not a case. It was some papers in a case." **The authorization code** has the regional prefix and is not in his own spring register, nor among the closed codes (**Book 6 plant**). His rule against speculation; *Query on return.* Earlier that day: off the **west cart** with a case "built for sixty" holding six sheets; **field files travel sealed** and he breaks the seal before **Halvern**, mid-dispute over a gutter measured in string-knots ("Permits and boundaries"). **Halvern's log**: the sweep came from regional on a code, not a name; a **bridge constable** walked it with a **pin lent from the drawer**; he found Torvin's by asking the carriers' clerk. "It wasn't cooked here. We only carry the pot." The cot upstairs. Night: the core's walls like a ladder; **his daughter, fourteen at midsummer**. Day 52: **Torvin's legal minimum** ("There's a room paid to the end of the week… It's what there is"; "Tell him about the oats"; "He pays on time. That's the most I'll say for anybody"). Walking the district: a town that settles its own quarrels; Paths used at work, which the Compact does not count; the clerk would tell anybody which day the boy posts. **"Circuit"** heard from fishwives and filed with dice and dogs; he stands at the foot of the yard lane long enough to read the prices and turns away. *My categories do not fit it well.* |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-005/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:19:| 31 | Footnote, Statute, Appendix | 3,915 | Day 54. The mender: "Wednesday." The **registry reading room** under the post, river side, three steps down, a sign nobody reads; **Halden**, nineteen years, three volumes (district handbook; the brittle supplementary register, uncopied in his time; the index, "wrong about a third of it"). **The desk-leg knock overhead**: he is reading under Coss's floor. False starts: (a) under sixteen is summoned through the standing-holder — closed, because Statute 14 revoked his standing and so he answers **in his own person from fourteen** (the notice made him his own man before the law); (b) retrieval needs the registering officer's countersignature — the clerk upstairs; (c) the index runs in a circle at section 40. Lira leaves at noon to listen in the district. **The find**: Part Four's definition → note 3 in the smallest print → **statute 19** → the **Second Appendix** (a loose page, the subheading he copied in Denvash, his word). The logic laid out; **read aloud four times like a load figure**, the last from the bottom up; **copied twice**. Coss's boots go past the high window. Halden: "Most of the people who walk out of here looking that pleased are wrong about something… come back. I'll find you the next book." Lira's news: single bread at Amrit's; the clerk; the foot of the yard lane; the skewer and "the circuit"; **nobody in the yards was asked anything**. |
