editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6800:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-15-| Brom | Iron Skin Path, Copper formal ("until somebody filed for him"); Iron-grade in practice. Third in Rooke's cohort; lost the Copper final to Lira by one beat in the fourth exchange, on the mended seam. The force-redirect seam is repaired (Rooke's nineteen exercises, four a week; he stops finishing the absorption and drives while still hard on the struck side). Recess sheet: "Nineteen. Round three. Four a week." Fit; the final's iced knee and strapped right knuckles are B4's and do not carry. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6804:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-19-| Hesk | At home in Denvash, his workshop "at the far end of the country" (B4 ch62). His last letter came by the evening coach on the twelfth: "…wrote 'keep looking.' In my day that was called respect… Sixteen suits you." (his guess from Cael's own letter, not knowledge; OWNER #10). Writes on "a war footing": nine letters in twelve weeks (B5's own; not in B4). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6805:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:20:| Vastin | The Archmarshal Vastin (his B4 title throughout, ch38–59). Last seen in B4 at the posting-house at the turn of the registry road on the evening of the twenty-fourth of Reaping, writing the file note and a four-sentence private letter to Bracken. His desk in the Compact's western administration (third floor, river side) is the source's, not B4's, and stands only until the text says otherwise. **No stated age** (§12 C2; OWNER #8, #17); career "forty years". His left hand "had begun to dislike evenings as well as mornings". [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6809:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:24:**Cael knows:** his six fragments, with their costs and deployment rules (the ch62 inventory: "Six and an anomaly. It isn't a seventh anything."); that the mechanism is integration of witnessed abilities under the stakes conditions; the line the four signed at Halcenvane the year before, the minute of three numbered rules (conditions not manufactured; a directed acquisition only within earnest engagement the other party begins, awake and directed; full cost written beforehand), for which *directed, open-eyed, or not at all* is this book's shorthand and never B4's wording; that Seln has functionally switched (the corridor on the twenty-seventh; the unchanged rotations; the recess counter sheet) and that "Gratitude is the leak"; that one unsigned slip of wing paper came to him inside a returned coursework folder on the night of the Copper final, learned and burned on the common-room coals, and that he and Karis alone know it; that Vastin wrote a note he believes says he is not an error (inferred, not seen; OWNER #10; "in a hand I'd wager signs its whole name"); that the Level 4 designation exists and nobody can trace it; that the fielding clause exists, with its text verbatim (sixth part, subsection four); the year's finding, "The system isn't confused about me"; and the tournament's three-year cycle and Norhold as this cycle's host. He does **not** know the Standard's mechanics yet (that comes in the map room); the exhibition provision's wording; the squad clause; Daeva beyond rumor; what Seln's reports said; or anything about the office above Vastin. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6823:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-38-- **Cael:** the Power Log (the old volume, near its last leaves; Hesk's bound volume arrives at the rest day), the year's inventory closed on the last night of term with Hesk's steel drafting pen; the observation notebook, with Hesk's reply and the birthday note behind its front board; Vell's letter (five short sentences, her mark and the circuit ledger's stamp); Hesk's travel clock (inaccurate; he sets it an hour fast during tournament weeks); a copy of Bracken's sanding habit; currency in marks (he does not spend much). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6824:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-39-- **Enrollment:** the demonstration provision of the assay clause, with one semester stamp, renewed (Bracken's line in the enrollment book on the twenty-second of Reaping; Gault's note of the twentieth: growth confirmed in five, the plate flat; the record keeps five capabilities, two of them public). Gault is the evaluator of record. Next term's sitting is already ruled on his calendar, the provision's half-yearly evaluation: *Panel of record: Gault, with two. Measured against: baseline (entry), and the note of the twentieth of Reaping.*; same instruments, checked on Fourth-days; the frame to get a new second notch. So the mill-town session (M2) is the provision's SECOND evaluation, not its third (§12 C8). The panel "travels" (a seals case with a handle) is the source's, to be staged in M1. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r2.stdout.log:6825:editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md-40-- **Delegation:** two wagons; travel roster of eleven (five competitors, Rooke, Gault, two third-year reserves, a wagoner, and S. Seln for *records and floor scheduling*). The roster line carries the registry name *Caelen Hesk-ward, 41-7843-V* once, so the schedule office's "C. Cael" reads as its abbreviation (§10 item 6). Fourteen of the hill's students are Silver and one is Gold (B4 ch8), and none is fielded; M1 says why in one sentence. Withrow and Bracken travel for the fourth meet and Norhold. Bracken's pouch is the delegation's letter route from Movement 3 on (Karis's information policy). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
