editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-003/review-editorial-prompt.md:177:He had stood in the station's bare room under the Arbiter with his mother's hand on his shoulder, and heard it read out in the clerk's flat voice. Iron Skin was a Path filed among the defensive ones, the kind that kept you whole. He was Copper, the first metal, with ten ranks to climb before anybody would look at him again.
