editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/review-cold.stdout.log:919:# Chapter 12 — Six Phases
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/review-cold.stdout.log:1180:He thought about the word the registry had given him in a hall at fourteen, with the Arbiter gone dark over his head after eleven seconds. Somebody had done a sum about him too, in front of everybody, and written the answer down. He had never once thought of answering it. He had only been getting on with things, a page at a time, in three columns, in the dark. Now, sitting beside her on the step, he wondered whether that was the same thing she meant, done more quietly.
