editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/review-cold.stdout.log:1475:# Chapter 13 — The Wrong Things
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/review-cold.stdout.log:1597:He did it at the crate desk with the door between the rooms open and the light from the yard window coming in grey, and he began at the very beginning. He took down the oldest notebook from the shelf, the one he had carried out of Denvash. He read his first pages of other people, the first fighters he had ever written down in Ardenmere, in the round anxious hand he had had at fourteen. Then he took the next volume, and the next, and came forward through the year to the grey book on his desk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/review-cold.stdout.log:1729:## CHAPTER — editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-14.md
