editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:949:## Numerical formula alignment
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:968:Method: the script strips the H1 and scene marks, removes Markdown emphasis, excludes fenced system notices from sentence/readability counts, treats each non-empty line as a written paragraph, and counts exact Markdown break lines as scene breaks. Sentences are split at terminal punctuation followed by whitespace and an opening quote/capital (or paragraph end), with common abbreviations and ellipses protected. Syllables use a vowel-group heuristic with silent-*e* and -*le* adjustments; proper nouns are treated the same as other words. Flesch results therefore have known estimator uncertainty. Written paragraphs and marked scene breaks are not equivalent to the source formula's ASR pause segmentation.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-003/recheck-r1.stdout.log:974:### Formula items not numerically measured
