editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:5586:    13	He went through the missing pieces methodically, the way he'd learned to audit a file when something about it didn't sit right: no preliminary risk assessment, though the certifying district — Denvash — had a functioning compliance office that produced these routinely for standard classifications. No residential compliance note beyond the bare expulsion language, though the standing-holder's guild status was explicitly flagged as at risk in that same expulsion notice, which should have triggered an automatic cross-reference to the guardian's own file. No indication that anyone had actually opened a formal case file at all, in the administrative sense — just a registration entry, a notice, and a flag, floating without the connective tissue a case this unusual should have generated.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:5606:    98	**SECRET:** All four were eliminated by the Guilds Compact on Architect-system instruction. The Arbiter system flags [SHATTERED] classifications to a deep-layer protocol that the Compact inherited without understanding it. When a [SHATTERED] appears, the Compact receives pressure — administrative, social, legal — to resolve the anomaly. They have always complied. Until Cael survives long enough to make compliance difficult.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:5610:   102	**Book 1-3 (what Cael believes):** His Fractured Path is a collection of unrelated ability shards — fragments of multiple Paths, none complete. The shards work, individually, but he has no Path declaration sequence, no tier advancement, no Arbiter guidance.
