editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9597:   221	He had read about it three times in the reference section on the eastern cities. He had known it was larger than Denvash, but he had not known what *larger* meant until he stood on the rise and looked. The river came in from the north, wide and slow and copper-coloured in the low sun, and bent through the middle of the valley like an arm.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-002/recheck-r1.stdout.log:9599:   223	On the far bank, in the crook of that arm, rose the Ranked core, walled and stepped, ring inside ring, each ring higher than the last. He could see the districts climbing toward the centre, Copper, he thought, and Iron, and Bronze, and at the very top something white with towers catching the last of the light. He had five pages in a notebook about one wall in Denvash. He could see six walls from here.
