    12	
    13	## Where we enter
    14	
    15	The morning after the last bout, four days before the academic year's close [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: season word struck; audit A1]. Four withdrawal forms squared on Bracken's counter. Seln has nothing to file.
    16	
    17	## What this movement is for
    18	
    19	The walk-out in its exact images, and its discipline is smallness. Then the empty desk, the machine's paperwork closing on air, four days of road on which the apparatus thins to nothing, the unmarked Line, and the first fire no Arbiter has measured. A deliberately quiet movement: its physical challenge is distance — the ford, the ridge with a blowing horse, scree switchbacks, a camp made from nothing.
    20	
    21	Consequential turns:
    22	- **Bracken's counter**: four leaves in the order they present (Lira, Brom, Cael; Seln absent from the sequence); *freely… and not by any officer of this institution*, longhand in the margin; **Karis's forfeiture read line by line** — certification retained ("they can only decline to count it"), the restricted-collection half-second, the key into its pigeonhole; Bracken off procedure; **Gault's last note**. The assistant's three things. Cael's room counted out.
    23	- **Lira's last class** — fifteen minutes of real notes, "Thank you. It's been a good class and you're a good teacher," the door; **Lira's window** (~1k) in the corridor; "Same door. Same leaving. Mine this time."
    24	- **Brom's three boxes**, three trips, help refused in shortening words, past the district officer's horse; **Ephram walks the last trip carrying nothing**; **Withrow at the gate: "Your files are in order. All four."**; **Rooke: "Doors open both ways."**; the watchers log it; the bluff road at dusk. "Four, closed complete. Tomorrow, the fifth."
    25	- **Not At His Desk** — *Seln simply wasn't at his desk the next morning.* The morning clerk's window; keys in a row; the summaries pinned eleven years later; the personnel query; **the apparatus window** — *what did he have*; fifteen years of true, empty product requisitioned. **Seln's window** (~3k): the east road in the dark; the last null report drafted and not filed; the case's history; looking back, badly; firewood for people who will be cold.
    26	- **The machine's week**: moot; executed against nobody; **pending jurisdiction**; the third visit to Hesk and a brass caliper bought at the marked price; **Vastin's window** (~1k) — the summary returned unannotated. The four on the road; one grey coat; **the crossroads camp**, the fire already built, water at forty paces; "I check."
    27	- **The Registry Line**: what the road still had, day by day; the last chartered waystation and its keeper ("You've boxes."); the last tier notice with a hay sum; **the last watcher's nod to Brom**; **the last station** (swept; roof mended by someone; the book that stops four years ago with its open line); five crossings, each in a sentence; **"You couldn't read me… Thanks for the eleven seconds."**; the Line, unmarked; **"Nobody's watching."**; the first night outside any jurisdiction; **the reply to Daeva** sent west with the post-rider at the ford; "Both promises ride east with me."; the first ridge — **"Nobody mentions that it's big."**
    28	- **Nine**: the shelf above the unnamed valley; the watch argument; Brom's load rule; Karis's field archive; Lira's route sheet; money; Ephram's absence once; **the inventory — nine, the blank where a name would be**; the anomaly's shorter procedure; **"Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch."**; **both poles left standing**; letters to Hesk and Vell with no return address; **the closing faceless window** and the new line; the last lines.
    29	
    30	## What must remain true / withheld
    31	
    32	- Protected: "Your files are in order. All four."; "Doors open both ways."; Gault's note; the Seln image as the chapter's first sentence; *pending jurisdiction*; Cael's reply to Daeva; "Nobody's watching."; "…it's big."; the inventory; *Still open. Still real. Patience.*; the Reydan/Daeva line; both poles; *active non-compliance, observation priority escalated* (bible form); the closing exchange.
    33	- **Five** cross the Line. Ephram stays. Withrow counts four.
    34	- The satchel was the eighteenth-birthday gift (not "since Ardenmere"); session nine was written at fifteen (§11 #8–9).
    35	- The faceless windows have no face, name, altitude or place. The monitoring apparatus does not know what Seln kept.
    36	- **No Quieting, no ruins, no Path-dead ground, no Oryn, no Tide practitioner.** The edge territories are only unadministered and big. Don't stage Lowmarch, Pike, the board or stillhounds (Book 7's).
    37	- Deployment past the Line: none. Shadow still sealed and still costing.
    38	- End on **the second day past the Line**; Book 7 Ch1's first log entry is "Second day past the Line."
    39	- Letters to Hesk and Vell are held, not sent (Book 7 hands them to a courier at a ford on day four).
    40	
    41	## What the author owns
    42	
    43	The road's incidents and weather; the waystation keeper's voice; which of the five crossings at the station gets the most room; the shelf's geography; the camp's humor; how the cart and horse are explained (hired to a first hold, or bought) — Book 7 never mentions them.
    44	
    45	## Where we leave pressure
    46	
    47	A fire in a territory no Arbiter has measured, a file behind them with a new sentence written by nobody, and for the first time since his Kindling nothing anywhere [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: replaces "in four years"; OWNER #9, #18; audit A9/C14] deciding what he is except him. Book 7 opens two days past the Line, on a road with ruts.

