   500	## 7. Progression plan
   501	
   502	### The system's vocabulary (front-loaded — formula §4)
   503	
   504	Book 6's progression vocabulary: tier, rank, Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver/Gold, Rank 1–9 (the edition shows no tenth) [B5-reconciled 2026-10-06: audit §F.5], rating,
   505	rated bout, bracket, Silver program, drill-book, flags, exchange, advancement review, standard
   506	panel, sigil frame, Arbiter, Arbiter protocol, evaluation, re-evaluation, classification,
   507	declaration, fragment, notice, integration, tier equivalent, engagement field, the public suite,
   508	the managed band, the covenant, the anomaly, enrollment, demonstration provision, the assay clause,
   509	nullification, suspension, asset-restriction, evaluation seat, evaluator of record.
   510	
   511	Target ~58 hits per 10k across the book, shaped like the formula (900 / 471 / 514 by thirds):
   512	**first third ~83/10k, middle ~44/10k, last ~48/10k.** Teach hardest in **M1–M3**: every fragment
   513	in use with its limit and cost; Lira's program as a visible ladder (Iron Rank One formal — the foot of Iron's seeding in the edition, B5 ch3:17, ch20:231 — toward the Silver bracket by rating at an advancement evaluation, not rank by rank [B5-reconciled 2026-10-06: audit §F.5]; the
   514	R7 third-year; the Silver assessor [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: ranks per audit C7, C8]; burst budgets); Brom's advancement procedure (Copper → Iron,
   515	standard panel, *anticipated*); Karis's tier and standing; chapter fourteen in full; Vastin's frames
   516	and evaluations; Daeva's Gold R3 statement; Withrow's nine categories. After M3 the system surfaces
   517	at turning points: the Silver R8 (M4), the Anchor notice and its integration (M5), the Blade notice
   518	(M8), the final inventory (M9).
   519	
   520	Any invented declaration text follows the Bible's standard format. New ability labels are new
   521	canon nouns: keep them few and flag them in the movement's state report.
