   166	
   167	The first ridge beyond the Line came at dusk on the fifth day, and they came up it in the last of the light with the horse blowing and nobody talking.
   168	
   169	The edge territories opened below.
   170	
   171	Unadministered, unmeasured, enormous: the continent's whole unmapped margin falling away east in ridge after ridge, blue and then bluer, into a dark that no station's light reached, no tier verified, no seal governed. There was a river down there somewhere, showing twice. There was smoke, once, a long way off, which meant people, and no way of knowing anything else about them. There were hills behind hills behind hills, and no road visible past the first eight miles of the one they were standing on.
