   282	
   283	The one to Vell was shorter. She had kept a ledger that rated him before any registry did, and he had written to her at the close of each year. He told her that the year had closed, and that he had been found lawful and revoked in one paragraph. He wrote that he did not think her ledger had ever been wrong about him, and that he was now somewhere it could not be checked.
   284	
