   312	
   313	Such a slip did not explain itself. It said what was to be entered, and a clerk did not ask it for its authority, any more than one asks a pen. The slip advised, and the entry was made as advised.
   314	
   315	The clerk dipped the pen and wrote a fifth line under the four, in the same ink.
