   257	Ten on a wall's count = the crew's six (Karis included — a wall counts who walks a site) + Teague's four; healers off it. Shares by count; the field Teague's; the reading Karis's; "Contract. Not more than that." The young one of Teague's crew died at the pass (Ch21), a stride outside Vastin's plane; Teague's lesson: "A wall keeps everyone behind it, and one of mine wasn't." "Next spring. Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes."

